title: pidly init
desc:25
Create a .pidly tree in a project that has none: the directory itself, a
seeded schema.md documenting the four structural header lines with an empty
project-field table, .pidly/README.md and the AGENTS.md summary via the same
code path as `pidly agents`, and ignore rules for the transient .lock files
and the .id fallback.

Nothing currently does this. new creates tickets inside a tracker that must
already exist, and agents writes documentation for a tracker it assumes is
there, so adopting pidly means hand-building the first directory.

Two things to decide while implementing:

Re-running on an existing tracker should refresh what is generated — the
summary, the reference, the ignore rules — and never touch schema.md, which
the project owns once it exists. That makes init safe to run after an upgrade
rather than a one-shot that punishes a second invocation.

Ignore rules probably belong in .pidly/.gitignore rather than the repo root,
so the tracker stays self-contained and can be copied into another project
without leaving stale entries in a file it does not own. This repo currently
does the opposite and would need migrating.
